# MapStruct Mappers

All mapping between adapter representations (REST DTOs, persistence entities, event payloads) and core domain models is done with **MapStruct** — never hand-rolled field-by-field mapping inside adapters, controllers, or services.

## Rules

- One mapper per adapter concern, living next to the adapter in a `mapper` package (e.g. `adapters/incoming/rest/mapper`, `adapters/outgoing/persistence/mapper`).
- Use CDI component model so mappers are injectable Quarkus beans:

```java
@Mapper(componentModel = "cdi")
public interface PositionRestMapper {
    PositionResponse toResponse(Position position);
    Position toDomain(CreatePositionRequest request);
}
```

- Domain models in `core/model` stay **free of MapStruct annotations** — mapping configuration (`@Mapping`, custom methods) belongs to the mapper in the adapter layer.
- Controllers delegate to use cases and mappers: map request DTO to `Command`, map `Result.Success` payload to response DTO. No mapping logic inline in controllers.
- Prefer explicit `@Mapping` for renames/derivations and default methods for small conversions; extract shared conversions (money, dates, enums) into a common mapper `uses = {...}`.
- Add `unmappedTargetPolicy = ReportingPolicy.ERROR` (or configure it globally) so silently dropped fields fail the build.
- Remember to add the MapStruct annotation processor to both `annotationProcessor` and `testAnnotationProcessor` configurations.
